CORE
JmlBasic
--function JmlBasic.identity --jml-source src/main/java/JmlBasic.java --unwind 5 -cp target/classes --proof-explanation
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^Proof explanation:$
^Per-property proof explanations:$
^.*\[assumption\].*JmlBasic\.java.*≥ 0
^.*\[assignment\].*#return_value.*=.*arg0i
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR
^.*FAILURE$
--
Phase-2 regression test for --proof-explanation on JBMC.

Reuses the JmlBasic.identity test class with `//@ requires x >= 0;
//@ ensures \\result >= x;`. Verifies the JBMC --proof-explanation
output:
- includes a "Proof explanation:" section header
- includes a "Per-property proof explanations:" section header
- the per-property slice for the JML postcondition contains both
  the precondition (rendered as [assumption] x >= 0) and the body
  assignment (rendered as [assignment] #return_value = arg0i)

This is a smoke test confirming the inherited word-level proof
machinery (CBMC PR #8927, cherry-picked at 04c20d4808/2c8b422f3b/
f067644cff) reaches Java verification through JBMC's CLI wiring
(commit adding --proof-explanation to JBMC_OPTIONS).
